'''The Lodge''' served as the rough-and-tumble saloon in [[Fort Ypso]] on the [[planet]] [[Vandor]]<ref name="Official Guide" /> that was owned by [[Tibbs Ospe]].<ref name="Tales from Vandor">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> It contained a gambling hall, [[droid]]-fighting arena, and hostel. A band comprised of a [[Nithorn]] singer and two [[human]]s also resided there. Adventurous [[scout]]s planned explorations at the bar, [[gambler]]s sought to reverse their fortunes at the [[sabacc]] table, and shadowed alcoves were perfect for conducting illicit business.<ref name="Official Guide" />

[[Han Solo]] first met [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] in the Lodge and they played a game of [[sabacc]] with a few other individuals. Among the spectators was [[Tam Posla]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Parts of the Lodge's design, including the droid-fighting pit, were based on unused concept art for [[Takodana Castle]] from [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']].<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

